Every new thread starts with every signal blocked (after patch 0040).
Only a thread whose mask differed from its creator's did; any other
started with its creator's mask, and on a system whose new thread sets
its own thread pointer, as Radix's does, a signal sent right after
pthread_create could run its handler before that, so pthread_self or
errno in the handler read through a null thread pointer. Now every
thread takes its mask, its creator's with patch 0040's changes, once its
TCB is set, as glibc's and musl's threads do, and the creator gets that
mask from the call that blocks its signals, as glibc does. Meant for
upstream.

diff --git a/options/internal/generic/threads.cpp b/options/internal/generic/threads.cpp
